OL,3,GFEATURES CThe mystery of the delayed
OL,4,Claunch for the new BBC regional news
OL,5,Cslot
OL,6,
OL,7,FARCHIVE: The TV Room
OL,8,
OL,9,F2nd September marks the 40th
OL,10,Fanniversary of a significantB relaunch
OL,11,Fof the Nine o'Clock News.
OL,12,
OL,13,FComputer graphics were introduced, new
OL,14,Ftitles and music were produced and the
OL,15,Fprogramme moved to a two-presenter
OL,16,Fformat.
OL,17,
OL,18,FBut look carefully at the listings for
OL,19,Fthat week and there is a little
OL,20,Fmystery.
OL,21,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBNat RadioCReg RadioFNat Sport
FL,123,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12202
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F122A1768698053
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G2/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CThe mystery of the delayed
OL,4,Claunch for the new BBC regional news
OL,5,Cslot
OL,6,
OL,7,FRadio Times shows that the new look
OL,8,FNine o'Clock News was supposed to be
OL,9,Ffollowed by a regional news bulletin.B
OL,10,
OL,11,FIn fact, the bulletin did not appear
OL,12,Funtil 6th January 1986.
OL,13,
OL,14,FRadio Times billed the regional news
OL,15,Ffor the first two weeks of September
OL,16,F1985 ` with the subsequent programme
OL,17,Fstarting at 9.30pm.
OL,18,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBNat RadioCReg RadioFNat Sport
FL,123,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12203
SC,0003
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F122A1768698053
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G3/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CThe mystery of the delayed
OL,4,Claunch for the new BBC regional news
OL,5,Cslot
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe regional news wasn't listed from
OL,8,F16th September and the following
OL,9,Fprogramme was billed with a 9.25pm
OL,10,Fstart.
OL,11,
OL,12,FSo what happened?
OL,13,
OL,14,FThe BBC had never provided mid-evening
OL,15,Fregional news bulletins previously.
OL,16,FHowever most English regions closed the
OL,17,Fnight with a regional news summary
OL,18,Fbefore English regional presentation
OL,19,Fwas dropped in 1980.
OL,20,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBNat RadioCReg RadioFNat Sport
FL,123,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12204
SC,0004
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F122A1768698053
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G4/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CThe mystery of the delayed
OL,4,Claunch for the new BBC regional news
OL,5,Cslot
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe nations still provided a bulletin
OL,8,Fat closedown ` albeit read
OL,9,Fout-of-vision by the announcer in
OL,10,FScotland and Wales.
OL,11,
OL,12,FBy 1985 most ITV regions had short
OL,13,Flocal summaries after News at Ten
OL,14,Falthough some were poorly produced. The
OL,15,Fannouncer would simply read a script
OL,16,Fwith no autocue or moving pictures.B
OL,17,
OL,18,FSo a regional news bulletin after the
OL,19,FNine o'Clock News seemed to be an
OL,20,Foverdue response by the BBC.
OL,21,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBNat RadioCReg RadioFNat Sport
FL,123,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12205
SC,0005
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F122A1768698053
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G5/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CThe mystery of the delayed
OL,4,Claunch for the new BBC regional news
OL,5,Cslot
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe move coincided with two other
OL,8,Fdevelopments.B
OL,9,
OL,10,FSo why was the plan for mid-evening
OL,11,Fbulletins suddenly postponed?
OL,12,
OL,13,FWere there practical issues such as
OL,14,Fdisputes over the rota? Were some
OL,15,Fregions initially unable to provide
OL,16,Fthem? Does anyone who worked in a
OL,17,Fregional newsroom in 1985 know what
OL,18,Fhappened?
OL,19,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBNat RadioCReg RadioFNat Sport
FL,123,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12206
SC,0006
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F122A1768698053
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G6/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CThe mystery of the delayed
OL,4,Claunch for the new BBC regional news
OL,5,Cslot
OL,6,
OL,7,FEither way the 2-minute bulletin
OL,8,Ffinally appeared in January 1986. It
OL,9,Fwas extended to around 3 minutes in
OL,10,F1995 and doubled in length when the
OL,11,Fnetwork news moved to 10pm in 2000.
OL,12,
OL,13,FBy the way, the schedule changes in
OL,14,F1985 meant routine opts on BBC Two in
OL,15,FEngland for the first time.
OL,16,
OL,17,FUntil then, they were exceptional ` for
OL,18,Finstance the early evening regional
OL,19,Fnews magazines moved to BBC Two during
OL,20,Fthe 1980 Olympics.
OL,21,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBNat RadioCReg RadioFNat Sport
FL,123,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12207
SC,0007
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F122A1768698053
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G7/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CThe mystery of the delayed
OL,4,Claunch for the new BBC regional news
OL,5,Cslot
OL,6,
OL,7,FApparently significant engineering work
OL,8,Fhad to take place in 1985 to make
OL,9,Fregular opting on BBC Two in England
OL,10,Fpractical. The channel's distribution
OL,11,Fnetwork was previously not tailored to
OL,12,Fallow for straightforward opting unlike
OL,13,Fthe BBC One distribution system.
OL,14,
OL,15,FIt is important not to confuse the
OL,16,Fability of each region to opt out on
OL,17,FBBC2 locally with "regional" trade test
OL,18,Ftransmissions which were a regular
OL,19,Foccurrence on the channel in the
OL,20,Fafternoon.B
OL,21,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBNat RadioCReg RadioFNat Sport
FL,123,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12208
SC,0008
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F122A1768698053
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G8/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CThe mystery of the delayed
OL,4,Claunch for the new BBC regional news
OL,5,Cslot
OL,6,
OL,7,FBirmingham, Cardiff and Glasgow
OL,8,Finserted Test Card G into the network
OL,9,Fdistribution circuit ` but these
OL,10,Fbroadcasts were seen across much of the
OL,11,Fcountry and not just their local areas.
OL,12,FB
OL,13,
OL,14,FThis took place so the BBC Two feed
OL,15,Ffrom London could be used to send
OL,16,Fprogramme material to the regions.B
OL,17,
OL,18,FBut back to the mystery of the
OL,19,Fmid-evening bulletin.
OL,20,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBNat RadioCReg RadioFNat Sport
FL,123,120,200,300,0,100
